   "kind": "thought",
   "data": {
    "text": "In Lekki-Ajah for a `120mm / 3h` storm:\n\n### 1. Baseline vs lagoon held 1m high\n\n> Tide is for this coastal area. `1.0m` is an assumed lagoon / sea level, not a forecast. Default in `get_aoi_info` is `-0.5m`.\n\n* Baseline - run `r_e02ffbbbe8c27b2d`:\n  * `buildings_flooded: 29137`\n  * `buildings_flooded_severe: 8230`\n  * `road_km_impassable: 384.7`\n  * `people_exposed: 88124`\n  * `flooded_area_km2: 21.8598`\n  * `max_depth_m: 2.051`\n\n* Tide lock `tide boundary_level_m: 1.0` - run `r_38f6b6843f5d0de1`:\n\n* Change alt - base:\n  * `buildings_flooded: +430` to `29567` - +1.5%\n  * `buildings_flooded_severe: +355` to `8585` - +4.3%\n  * `buildings_flooded_own_cell: +226` to `12646`\n  * `road_km_impassable: +45.371` to `430.071` - +11.8%\n  * `people_exposed: +2088` to `90212`\n  * `flooded_area_km2: +6.6476` to `28.5074` - +30%\n  * `max_depth_m: +0.013` to `2.064`\n\nMechanism in the water budget:\n\n* `stored_volume_end_m3: +6491847.2`\n* `boundary_outflow_m3: -6536163.3` to `-4992827.9`\n\ni.e. the high boundary blocks outflow and pushes lagoon water into the domain. This is a planning model, not a forecast.\n\nImpact is not uniform. Example `area:Lekki Phase 1:buildings_flooded`:\n\n* baseline `1555`, tide-lock `1555` - no change\n* `area:Lekki Phase 1:max_depth_m: 1.296` in both\n* `area:Lekki Phase 1:road_km_impassable: 18.468` in both\n\nThe +430 flooded buildings and +45 km impassable road occur elsewhere in the domain, with flooded area spreading by ~6.6 km2.\n\n### 2. Evacuation route to nearest shelter\n\nOrigin tested: `Lekki Phase 1 [3.47674,6.44154]` to nearest shelter, evaluated at 1h `t_s=3600` and at peak `t_s=10200`.\n\nAt 1h:\n\n* baseline `rt_47a5d02258e5`: `reachable: true` to `Lekki British School (candidate shelter (assumed))`, `length_km: 0.865`, `eta_min: 13.0`\n* tide lock `rt_89bb17a910f4`: `reachable: true` to same shelter, same path, `length_km: 0.865`, `eta_min: 13.0`\n\nRoute geometry unchanged, but network redundancy collapses:\n\n* `edges_removed: 20` baseline vs `344` tide-lock\n\nAt peak `10200s`:\n\n* baseline `rt_cd2e1d1b6360`: `reachable: false`\n* tide lock `rt_a9f9f35f77d2`: `reachable: false`\n* `edges_removed: 2563` vs `2886` - ~323 more links cut under tide lock.\n\nEngineering read: tide lock adds modest building count but large area + road impact, and leaves no passable late evacuation from this origin in either case. Evacuation would have to use the early ~1h window, when the tide-lock case has far fewer alternate roads."
